# Formats what is being committed, and reports on it. Never blocks on style.
#
# `lint-staged` is here for correctness, not for speed (ADR 0026 §8): oxfmt and
# oxlint together take 0.72 s over the WHOLE repository, so narrowing them saves
# nothing. What narrowing buys is that a hook which writes files writes only the
# ones being committed — running oxfmt across the tree from here would pull
# unstaged work into somebody's commit.
#
# Typecheck and tests are deliberately absent: they are 16 of the 17 seconds and
# they run on pre-push, which is the moment the work starts to matter to anyone
# else.
npx lint-staged
